=== PicasaImport ===
Contributors: Bueltge
Donate link: http://bueltge.de/wunschliste/
Tags: picasa, rss, import, php, post, images, google
Requires at least: 1.5

Import the RSS-Feed from your Picasa-Web-Albums in your WP-Blog.

== Description ==

= This plugin is not developed and maintained. =

List a RSS-Feed from Picasa-Web-Albums in your WP-Blog.

Please visit [the official website](http://bueltge.de/wp-picasaimport-plugin/448/ "PicasaImport") for further details and the latest information on this plugin.

== Installation ==
1. Unpack the download-package
1. Upload the folder include files to the `/wp-content/plugins/` directory
1. Activate the plugin through the 'Plugins' menu in WordPress
1. create a new page or post with php-code
* (this only possiblity with php-plugin, example: [Exec-PHP](http://bluesome.net/post/2005/08/18/50/ "Exec-PHP")
1. the code in the page/post is: `<?php picasaimport($display, $url); ?>`
* `$display` = How any entry?
* `$url` = URL of the Picasa-Web-Album-Feed (without: `&alt=rss&hl=de`, end with: `=album`)
* **Example:**    `<?php picasaimport(2, "http://picasaweb.google.com/data/feed/base/user/example?kind=album") ?>`

See on [the official website](http://bueltge.de/wp-picasaimport-plugin/448/ "PicasaImport").

== Frequently Asked Questions ==

= You see the image double =
Check your Picasa-URL, she must end with `=album`, without `&alt=rss& . . .`

